# Keep shell scripts LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# These scripts are the deployment path for the headless VPS (service start,
# build, watchdog). A CRLF shell script fails there with
# "$'\r': command not found", which reads like a missing file rather than a line
# ending problem, and the failure is silent enough to cost an evening.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Keep Go sources LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# gofmt compares the whole file, so a CRLF working copy makes `gofmt -l` list
# the entire Go tree on Windows even though the repository (and CI, which
# checks out LF) is clean. An agent verifying formatting then sees ~110 false
# positives and cannot tell its own unformatted file from the pack.
*.go text eol=lf
